<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL RESULT.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the first  game in the best-of-three ice hockey world championship pool A final on Sunday:</p>
<p>Canada 2 Sweden 3 (1-1 0-1 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Canada - Mark Recchi (10:54), Anson Carter (59:22).</p>
<p>Sweden - Jonas Hoglund (15:29), Niklas Sundblad (35:47), Marcus Thuresson (56:05).</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 20 minutes, Sweden 20 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,300.</p>
<p>Sweden lead final series 1-0.</p>
<p>The second game is on Tuesday with the third, if necessary, on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
